<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">Events</h2><ol class="day-events yr-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/emilio-aguinaldo" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/emilio-aguinaldo.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/january-23">23 January</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">The First Philippine Republic is inaugurated at Malolos</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Philippine Republic was established at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malolos">Malolos</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bulacan">Bulacan</a>, under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malolos-constitution">Malolos Constitution</a>, succeeding the revolutionary government, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emilio-aguinaldo">Emilio Aguinaldo</a> as its first president. No foreign power recognised it, but it remained a de facto government.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malolos">Malolos</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malolos-constitution">Malolos Constitution</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emilio-aguinaldo">Emilio Aguinaldo</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/manila" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/manila.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/february-4">4 February</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Philippine-American War breaks out in Manila</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Shots exchanged between American and Filipino troops sparked war between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> and the Philippine Republic. Officially ended in 1902, the conflict killed some 200,000 or more Filipino civilians.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manila">Manila</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/philippine-american-war" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/philippine-american-war.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/march-31">31 March</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">American forces capture Malolos, capital of the Philippine Republic</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The division of General <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arthur-macarthur-jr">Arthur MacArthur Jr.</a> advanced along the Manila-Dagupan Railway and took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malolos">Malolos</a>, where the First Philippine Republic had been established. The Aguinaldo government had already moved its seat to San Isidro, Nueva Ecija.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/united-states">United States</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malolos">Malolos</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philippine-american-war">Philippine–American War</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emilio-aguinaldo">Aguinaldo</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/october-11">11 October</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">The Second Boer War begins in South Africa</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">War broke out when <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> let a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boers">Boer</a> ultimatum expire. In the three-year conflict that followed, British <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/concentration-camp">concentration camps</a> saw the deaths of about 26,000 Boer women and children and many thousands of black Africans.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/british-empire">British Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-boer-war">Second Boer War</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-africa">South Africa</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/ladysmith-kwazulu-natal" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ladysmith-kwazulu-natal.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/november-2">2 November</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">The Boers begin the siege of Ladysmith</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-boer-war">Second Boer War</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boers">Boer</a> forces besieged the British garrison at Ladysmith in Natal. The siege lasted 118 days, until Sir Redvers Buller's army relieved the garrison on 28 February 1900 after costly battles at Colenso and Spion Kop.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ladysmith-kwazulu-natal">Ladysmith</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-boer-war">Second Boer War</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boers">Boers</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/philippine-american-war" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/philippine-american-war.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/december-2">2 December</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">A Filipino rearguard holds Tirad Pass to cover Aguinaldo's escape</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">In northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/luzon">Luzon</a>, a 60-man Filipino rearguard under Brigadier General Gregorio del Pilar was overcome by more than 500 Americans, but delayed their advance long enough for President <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emilio-aguinaldo">Emilio Aguinaldo</a> and his troops to escape.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philippine-american-war">Philippine–American War</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emilio-aguinaldo">Emilio Aguinaldo</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Peace</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/bloemfontein-conference">Bloemfontein Conference</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Bloemfontein Conference was a meeting held in Bloemfontein from 31 May to 5 June 1899 between Paul Kruger, president of the South African Republic, and Alfred Milner, the British High Commissioner, hosted by President Steyn of the Orange Free State.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/kiram-bates-treaty" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kiram-bates-treaty.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Treaty</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/kiram-bates-treaty">Kiram-Bates Treaty</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Kiram-Bates Treaty was an agreement signed in August 1899 between the United States, represented by General John C. Bates, and Sultan Jamalul Kiram II of Sulu.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-magersfontein" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-magersfontein.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Battle</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-magersfontein">Battle of Magersfontein</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Battle of Magersfontein was fought on 11 December 1899 near Kimberley, in the Second Boer War, when Boer forces under Piet Cronjé and Koos de la Rey, dug into trenches at the foot of the hills, repulsed a British attack under Lord Methuen.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/tripartite-convention-1899" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tripartite-convention-1899.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Treaty</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/tripartite-convention-1899">Tripartite Convention (1899)</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Tripartite Convention of 1899 partitioned the Samoan Islands between Germany and the United States.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/voulet-chanoine-mission" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/voulet-chanoine-mission.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Campaign</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/voulet-chanoine-mission">Voulet–Chanoine Mission</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Voulet–Chanoine Mission was a French military expedition of 1899 led by Captains Paul Voulet and Julien Chanoine, sent from French Sudan to conquer the territory towards Lake Chad.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Treaty</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/anglo-kuwaiti-agreement-of-1899">Anglo-Kuwaiti Agreement of 1899</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Anglo-Kuwaiti Agreement of 23 January 1899 was a secret treaty between Britain and Mubarak al-Sabah, ruler of Kuwait.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Battle</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-umm-diwaykarat">Battle of Umm Diwaykarat</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Battle of Umm Diwaykarat was fought on 24 November 1899 in Kordofan, Sudan, and ended the Mahdist State.</p></div></li></ol></section>
