<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">In the profiles</h2><ul class="yr-prof"><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/wadai-empire"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Wadai%20Empire.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Wadai Empire</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">An Anglo-French convention places Wadai in the French sphere</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/grand-duchy-of-hesse"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Grand%20Duchy%20of%20Hesse.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Grand Duchy of Hesse</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Ernest Louis founds the Darmstadt Artists' Colony</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/kingdom-of-bunyoro"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Kingdom%20of%20Bunyoro.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Kingdom of Bunyoro</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Kabalega is captured in Lango and exiled to the Seychelles</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/south-african-republic"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/South%20African%20Republic.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>South African Republic</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Second Boer War begins after a Transvaal ultimatum expires</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/movement/nahda"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Nahda.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Nahda</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Muhammad Abduh becomes Grand Mufti of Egypt; Qasim Amin publishes The Liberation of Women</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/culture/ainu"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Ainu.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Ainu</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Hokkaido Former Aborigines Protection Act takes Ainu land and aims to erase Ainu culture and identity</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/kingdom-of-dagbon"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Kingdom%20of%20Dagbon.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Kingdom of Dagbon</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Yaa Naa Andani II dies in August; the British and Germans split Dagbon between German Togoland and the Gold Coast.</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/ideology/socialism"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Socialism.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Socialism</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Australian Labor Party forms the first socialist government in the world, in the Colony of Queensland, for one week</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/city/babylon"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Babylon.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Babylon</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Robert Koldewey begins the first scientific excavations</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/city/hue"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Hu%E1%BA%BF.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Huế</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Phú Xuân is officially renamed Huế under French rule</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/work/ishtar-gate"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Ishtar%20Gate.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Ishtar Gate</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Robert Koldewey began his part in the excavation of Babylon</span></li></ul></section>
